{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Elohim</b> — I have mentioned several explanations, for the force of the noun [i.e., divine name] applies to both past and future. So too here: אלהים דבר בקדשו — He spoke in His holiness, by way of prophecy to Samuel: that My kingdom shall stand over Israel, not like the kingdom of Saul." "<b>Shechem</b> — it is the city. So too Succoth." "<b>I will divide them</b> — that it shall always be in His portion, and I will appoint over it my appointees."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:23.552937028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}